# Formal proofs — `tpt-chrysalis-hal` deterministic wedge

This directory records the formal-verification intent for the Phase 1 `no_std`
HAL control-loop critical path (TODO.md Phase 1, lines 51–52).

The proof harnesses live in `crates/out-chrysalis-verify/` (an isolated crate
*excluded* from the workspace so the shippable HAL stays publish-clean). They
are written against the `cfg(kani)` proof-tooling cfg declared in the root
`Cargo.toml`, using the open-source Kani verifier; `tpt-telos` is the
ecosystem's verification integration point that drives the same harnesses.

## `dispense.telos`

The canonical proof: given an arbitrary `DispenseCommand`, the volume is
bounded by `HAL_LIMITS` (no overflow / over-dispense), the actuation timing
uses saturating arithmetic (no underflow / panic), and `Copy` command values
survive the control loop without corruption (no uninitialized reads).

Harness mapping (in `crates/out-chrysalis-verify/src/lib.rs`):

| Proof | Property | Harness |
|---|---|---|
| 1  | In-limits dispense never reported `OutOfLimits` | `proof_dispense_in_limits_accepted` |
| 1b | Over-limit volume always flagged | `proof_dispense_over_limit_rejected` |
| 2  | Timing never underflows / panics | `proof_timing_no_underflow` |
| 3  | `Copy` command lossless round-trip | `proof_command_copy_roundtrip` |
| 4  | Race-freedom (structural: `&mut self`, no shared mutability) | doc + compile-time guarantees |

Run with `cargo kani` (Kani toolchain installed). The same properties are
sampled concretely by `tests/bounded_checks.rs` under plain `cargo test`.
